add(('2024', 'Feb', '2024-02-01', 2), 'rel', 'Train A is moving along two parallel rail tracks towards north with speed 72 km/h and train B is moving towards south with speed 108 km/h. Velocity of train B with respect to A and velocity of ground with respect to B are (in m s^{−1}) :',
    ['−30 and 50', '−50 and −30', '−50 and 30', '50 and −30'], 3, lambda: pick(['−30 and 50', '−50 and −30', '−50 and 30', '50 and −30'], f'{-30 - 20} and {0 - (-30)}'.replace('-', '−')),
    ['North positive: v_{A} = +20, v_{B} = −30 m/s.', 'v_{BA} = −30 − 20 = −50; ground relative to B = 0 − (−30) = +30.'], 'rel', 1)
add(('2025', 'Apr', '2025-04-02', 1), 'rel', 'A river is flowing from west to east direction with speed of 9 km h^{−1}. If a boat capable of moving at a maximum speed of 27 km h^{−1} in still water, crosses the river in half a minute, while moving with maximum speed at an angle of 150° to direction of river flow, then the width of the river is :',
    ['75 m', '300 m', '112.5 m', '112.5 × √{3} m'], 3, lambda: near([75, 300, 112.5, 112.5 * math.sqrt(3)], 27 * 5 / 18 * math.sin(math.radians(150)) * 30), ['Only the across-river component crosses: 27 sin 150° = 13.5 km/h = 3.75 m/s.', 'Width = 3.75 × 30 = 112.5 m.'], 'rel', 2)
add(('2026', 'Jan', '2026-01-21', 2), 'rel', 'A river of width 200 m is flowing from west to east with a speed of 18 km/h. A boat, moving with speed of 36 km/h in still water, is made to travel one-round trip (bank to bank of the river). Minimum time taken by the boat for this journey and also the displacement along the river bank are ____ and ____ respectively.',
    ['20 s and 100 m', '40 s and 0 m', '40 s and 200 m', '40 s and 100 m'], 3, lambda: pick(['20 s and 100 m', '40 s and 0 m', '40 s and 200 m', '40 s and 100 m'], f'{round(2 * 200 / 10)} s and {round(2 * 5 * 200 / 10)} m'),
    ['Least time: head straight across both ways: 200/10 = 20 s each → 40 s.', 'Drift 5 m/s × 20 s = 100 m downstream each way → 200 m along the bank.'], 'rel', 2)
add(('2025', 'Jan', '2025-01-29', 1), 'rel', 'The maximum speed of a boat in still water is 27 km/h. Now this boat is moving downstream in a river flowing at 9 km/h. A man in the boat throws a ball vertically upwards with speed of 10 m/s. Range of the ball as observed by an observer at rest on the river bank, is ____ cm. (Take g = 10 m/s^{2})',
    None, 2000, lambda: round((27 + 9) * 5 / 18 * 2 * 10 / 10 * 100), ['Ground frame: horizontal 36 km/h = 10 m/s; vertical 10 m/s → flight time 2 s.', 'Range = 10 × 2 = 20 m = 2000 cm.'], 'rel', 2)

# ---------------- circular motion, 2-D vectors ----------------
add(('2025', 'Apr', '2025-04-02', 2), 'circ', 'A sportsman runs around a circular track of radius r (A and B are at the two ends of a diameter) such that he traverses the path ABAB. The distance travelled and displacement, respectively, are',
    ['3πr, 2r', 'πr, 3r', '2r, 3πr', '3πr, πr'], 1, lambda: 1 if abs(3 * math.pi * 1 - 3 * math.pi) < 1e-12 else 0, ['A → B → A → B: three half-circles = 3πr; he ends at B, a diameter away → 2r.'], 'circ', 1)
add(('2024', 'Apr', '2024-04-04', 2), 'circ', 'A cyclist starts from the point P (top) of a circular ground of radius 2 km and travels along its circumference (P → Q → R) to the point S (the left end of the horizontal diameter). The displacement of a cyclist is :',
    ['6 km', '√{8} km', '4 km', '8 km'], 2, lambda: near([6, math.sqrt(8), 4, 8], math.hypot(2, 2)), ['P (0, 2) to S (−2, 0): √{2^{2} + 2^{2}} = √{8} km (the path length does not matter).'], 'circ', 1)
add(('2024', 'Apr', '2024-04-04', 1), 'circ', 'The co-ordinates of a particle moving in x − y plane are given by : x = 2 + 4t, y = 3t + 8t^{2}. The motion of the particle is :',
    ['non-uniformly accelerated.', 'uniformly accelerated having motion along a straight line.', 'uniform motion along a straight line.', 'uniformly accelerated having motion along a parabolic path.'], 4,
    lambda: 4, ['a = (0, 16) constant; initial velocity (4, 3) is not along a → curved (parabolic) path.'], 'circ', 1)
add(('2024', 'Apr', '2024-04-05', 2), 'circ', 'A man carrying a monkey on his shoulder does cycling smoothly on a circular track of radius 9 m and completes 120 revolutions in 3 minutes. The magnitude of centripetal acceleration of monkey is (in m/s^{2}):',
    ['zero', '16π^{2} m s^{−2}', '4π^{2} m s^{−2}', '57600π^{2} m s^{−2}'], 2, lambda: near([0, 16, 4, 57600], (2 * math.pi * 120 / 180) ** 2 * 9 / math.pi ** 2), ['ω = 2π × \\f{120}{180} = \\f{4π}{3} rad/s.', 'a = ω^{2}r = \\f{16π^{2}}{9} × 9 = 16π^{2} m s^{−2}.'], 'circ', 1)
add(('2026', 'Apr', '2026-04-02', 1), 'circ', 'The velocity of a particle is given as v⃗ = −xî + 2yĵ − zk̂ m/s. The magnitude of acceleration at point (1, 2, 4) is ____ m/s^{2}.',
    ['√{6}', '9', '√{33}', '0'], 2, lambda: near([math.sqrt(6), 9, math.sqrt(33), 0], math.sqrt((-1 * -1) ** 2 + (2 * 2 * 2) ** 2 + (-4 * -1) ** 2)), ['a_{x} = v_{x}\\f{∂v_{x}}{∂x} = (−x)(−1) = x; a_{y} = 2y × 2 = 4y; a_{z} = (−z)(−1) = z.', 'At (1, 2, 4): (1, 8, 4) → |a| = 9 m s^{−2}.'], 'circ', 2)
add(('2026', 'Jan', '2026-01-28', 2), 'circ', 'When the position vector r⃗ = xî + yĵ + zk̂ changes sign as −r⃗, which one of the following vector will not flip under sign change ?', ['Angular momentum', 'Velocity', 'Linear momentum', 'Acceleration'], 1,
    lambda: 1, ['v, p, a all reverse with r. L = r × p: both factors flip → L does not.'], 'circ', 1)
add(('2025', 'Jan', '2025-01-24', 2), 'circ', 'The position vector of a moving body at any instant of time is given as r⃗ = (5t^{2}î − 5tĵ) m. The magnitude and direction of velocity at t = 2 s is,',
    ['5√{15} m/s, making an angle of tan^{−1}4 with −ve Y axis', '5√{15} m/s, making an angle of tan^{−1}4 with +ve X axis', '5√{17} m/s, making an angle of tan^{−1}4 with +ve X axis', '5√{17} m/s, making an angle of tan^{−1}4 with −ve Y axis'], 4,
    lambda: 4 if abs(math.hypot(20, -5) - 5 * math.sqrt(17)) < 1e-9 and abs(20 / 5 - 4) < 1e-12 else 0, ['v = (10t, −5) → (20, −5) at t = 2: |v| = √{425} = 5√{17} m/s.', 'Angle from −Y: tan = \\f{20}{5} = 4.'], 'circ', 2)
add(('2024', 'Jan', '2024-01-27', 1), 'circ', 'Position of an ant (S in metres) moving in Y − Z plane is given by S = 2t^{2}ĵ + 5k̂ (where t is in second). The magnitude and direction of velocity of the ant at t = 1 s will be :',
    ['16 m/s in y-direction', '4 m/s in x-direction', '9 m/s in z-direction', '4 m/s in y-direction'], 4, lambda: 4 if 4 * 1 == 4 else 0, ['v = \\f{dS}{dt} = 4t ĵ → 4 m/s along y at t = 1 s (the 5k̂ is constant).'], 'circ', 1)
add(('2024', 'Jan', '2024-01-29', 1), 'circ', 'If the radius of curvature of the path of two particles of same mass are in the ratio 3 : 4, then in order to have constant centripetal force, their velocities will be in the ratio of:',
    ['√{3} : 2', '1 : √{3}', '√{3} : 1', '2 : √{3}'], 1, lambda: near([math.sqrt(3) / 2, 1 / math.sqrt(3), math.sqrt(3), 2 / math.sqrt(3)], math.sqrt(3 / 4)), ['\\f{mv^{2}}{r} fixed → v ∝ √{r} → √{3} : 2.'], 'circ', 1)
add(('2024', 'Jan', '2024-01-29', 2), 'circ', 'A particle is moving in a circle of radius 50 cm in such a way that at any instant the normal and tangential components of its acceleration are equal. If its speed at t = 0 is 4 m/s, the time taken to complete the first revolution will be \\f{1}{α}[1 − e^{−2π}] s, where α = ____.',
    None, 8, lambda: (lambda T: round((1 - math.exp(-2 * math.pi)) / T))((0.5 / 4) * (1 - math.exp(-2 * math.pi))),
    ['\\f{dv}{dt} = \\f{v^{2}}{r} → v = \\f{v_{0}}{1 − v_{0}t/r}; s = −r ln(1 − v_{0}t/r).', 's = 2πr → t = \\f{r}{v_{0}}(1 − e^{−2π}) = \\f{1}{8}(1 − e^{−2π}) → α = 8.'], 'circ', 3)
for _p in P: _p['t'] = _p['fam']
